\title{One instance-path comparison: 65,363 machine steps against 222 for gruszka}
\taxon{Example}
\date{2026-11-24}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{queclr}
\tag{machine}
\tag{performance}
\meta{origin}{docs/research/profiles/P8.md}
\import{base-macros}

\p{The traced unit of profile P8 that shows where the machine loses on Mathlib. Source: [rep-P8](rep-P8), section 4.1; [the profiling session](ses-JRSD). Counts are steps of each checker on the unit \code{\verb~|AlgebraicGeometry.Spec.sheafedSpaceMap_hom_c_app~}; machine with the switch set \code{\verb~|warm,gated,expect~}, traced on the JVM with one worker.}
\pre{\verb~|
-- while the type of the theorem is inferred:
Module R R inst ..   =?=   Module R R inst' ..
-- the instance arguments are two paths to one structure
Semiring.toAddCommMonoid R (CommSemiring.toSemiring ..)
AddCommGroup.toAddCommMonoid R (Ring.toAddCommGroup ..)
-- field 1 of both is add_comm, a proof; its type on each side:
(a b : R) -> a + b = b + a      -- with + through one path, and through the other
~}
\table{
\tr{\th{Checker}\th{Steps}\th{Unfoldings}\th{Comparisons}}
\tr{\td{machine, \code{\verb~|warm,gated,expect~}}\td{65,363}\td{5,359}\td{2,227 and 1,868 pair hits; 2,086 proof-irrelevance steps}}
\tr{\td{machine with \code{\verb~|facts~}}\td{62,106}\td{5,359}\td{892 proof-irrelevance steps}}
\tr{\td{machine with \code{\verb~|facts~} and \code{\verb~|skipargs~}}\td{8,091}\td{589}\td{298; 29 proof-irrelevance steps}}
\tr{\td{machine with \code{\verb~|facts,probes~} and \code{\verb~|congruence,skipargs~}}\td{3,849}\td{221}\td{187; 10 proof-irrelevance steps}}
\tr{\td{gruszka}\td{222}\td{10}\td{25 calls, 14 cache hits}}
\tr{\td{nano-lean}\td{162}\td{9}\td{82 calls, 76 answered by pointer equality}}
}
\ul{
\li{Lazy delta unfolds both paths and structure eta compares the fields. Every proof field goes through proof irrelevance, which, as in the official kernel, infers both types and compares them: the statements of the laws, in which every \code{\verb~|+~}, \code{\verb~|*~} and \code{\verb~|0~} is unfolded again on both sides.}
\li{\code{\verb~|HAdd.hAdd~}, \code{\verb~|instHAdd~}, \code{\verb~|Add.add~} and \code{\verb~|AddMonoid.toAdd~} are projection functions with the hint abbrev, so the official order does not try their arguments first.}
\li{The extreme case is an instance field: \code{\verb~|AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.instAddCommGroupEllAdicCohomology._proof_21~} costs the machine 2,204,336 steps and 2.91 G instructions, gruszka 144 steps and 90,700 instructions; with \code{\verb~|skipargs~} 604 steps, with both options 175.}
}
\p{Used by [40 percent of the machine work on Mathlib is the official way of comparing proofs](ins-HPBW).}
\p{See also: [the two proof-comparison shortcuts](design-proof-comparison-shortcuts).}
